{"kind":"promise","text":"I will re-anchor the fifteen pages semantically, not by substitution, on a fresh request/docs-behavior-reanchor worktree.\n\nWhat I take the work to be. For each page, read what it actually claims about behaviour and choose the live non-stale artifacts at the real shipped paths that carry that behaviour. My survey computed a successor per citation, and that mapping is exactly what this request forbids me from applying: several of those successors are themselves stale, four would move a page from one `.` artifact to another, and several point into spike paths for behaviour that ships from internal/. The survey was a list of what is broken, not a plan for fixing it.\n\nOn the count, you are right and my wording was not. I wrote fourteen pages resting on retired artifacts and one citing an event that is not in the log, which is fifteen entries described as fourteen. Covering all fifteen is correct.\n\nOn sequencing. I will hold docs/how-to/configure-an-agent.md, docs/reference/mcp/status.md and docs/reference/mcp/wait.md until the addressed-inbox work lands, and anchor them to its final artifacts rather than to a moving branch. If that work has not landed by the time the other twelve are ready, I will say so rather than quietly anchoring to something provisional or quietly shipping twelve as though it were fifteen — the choice between waiting and splitting the head is yours, and I will bring it back with the state of the inbox line rather than deciding it myself.\n\nOne page needs a decision rather than a lookup: notes/2026-08-07-bootstrap-task-cycle.md cites b739ae18, which resolves to no event at all. There is nothing to supersede and nothing to follow, so the citation cannot be repaired by choosing a better artifact — it has to be replaced by whatever the note actually rests on, or removed if the note rests on nothing durable. I will say which I did and why.\n\nI will publish one exact-head docs artifact resting on this request, this promise, and every behaviour artifact I select, run make docs and git diff --check, and request an independent exact-head review covering architecture, security and simplification before any merge.","body":{"branch":"request/docs-behavior-reanchor"}}